 "result_text": "`Chain.from_json(chain.to_json())` now works for your example: the round trip rebuilds the `is_in` predicate, and the re-serialised JSON matches the original. I only ran that one check, not the test suite.\n\nThe cause was in `maybe_filter_dict_from_json` in `graphistry/compute/ast.py`. It called `ASTPredicate.from_json`, the generic base-class method, which can't tell which predicate class a JSON dict describes. It now calls the dispatcher in `graphistry/compute/predicates/from_json.py`, which picks the right class from the `type` field. That function is used for node and edge matches, including `edge_match`. I added the import next to the existing `filter_by_dict` import.\n\nI didn't add a test, as you asked.",
